course: dictionary
lesson: 10925
title: Voluntary: done by choice
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A voluntary action is one you choose to do. Nobody forces you. The word comes from "volunteer", someone who offers to help. Voluntary means done because you want to, not because you are made to.
explain: Look at the clues around the word. «Voluntary severance» means being paid to leave one's job, so the worker chooses to leave and is paid for it. The word voluntary tells you the choice is theirs. Ask yourself: could someone be made to do this? If not, voluntary is probably the right meaning.
explain: Voluntary can describe groups, not just actions. «The Commonwealth of Nations is a voluntary group of 56 countries» means the countries chose to join together. Nobody forced them.
explain: Voluntary also has a science meaning. A voluntary movement is one you control on purpose, like moving your arm. Your heartbeat is not voluntary, because it keeps going without you deciding anything.
fact: Voluntary means done because you want to, not because you are forced.
fact: Voluntary work is done without being paid, to help others.
fact: A voluntary club is one you choose to join.
fact: A volunteer is a person who offers to do voluntary work.
fact: «Voluntarily» is the adverb: it means in a voluntary way, by choice.
exercise: «Ella does voluntary work at the park, helping to pick up litter.» Why is her work voluntary? | She is forced to do it by her teacher | She must do it every day by law | She is paid a lot of money for it | *She chooses to do it without being paid
exercise: Which of these is a voluntary club? | Paying a fine for a parking ticket | Going to bed when you are told | Brushing your teeth because a parent makes you | *Joining the choir because you love singing
exercise: Which of these is a voluntary movement in science? | Your stomach digesting your lunch | Your heart beating | *Waving your hand on purpose | Blinking when something flies at your eye
test: Which word means done by choice, not forced? | Mandatory | *Voluntary | Required | Compulsory
test: «Voluntary severance» means being paid to leave one's job. Why is this called voluntary? | The worker is sacked and must go | *The worker chooses to leave | The worker is paid nothing at all | The worker is forced to stay forever
exam: Lucy says voluntarily is the adverb of voluntary. Which sentence uses it correctly? | She stayed late volunteer, to help tidy the library | *She stayed late voluntarily, to help tidy the library | She stayed late voluntary, to help tidy the library
